{
  "chapter": "reliability/timeouts-and-retries",
  "tier": "drill",
  "notes": [
    "Retry at exactly one layer per failure class, and set the others to one attempt.",
    "Nested retries multiply; they never add, which is why a class with three owners is",
    "twenty-seven provider calls for one logical step.",
    "modelRetries is the fourth layer: the model reads a tool error in its transcript and",
    "calls the tool again. It is not configured here, it multiplies anyway, and collapsing",
    "the other three cannot bound it.",
    "The deadline belongs to the run, not the call. Each call gets the smaller of its own",
    "timeout and a reserved share of what remains, so the run can still finish and write",
    "its result.",
    "A per-call cap bounds nothing globally. The retry budget is a share of traffic over a",
    "rolling window, and when it is spent the failure passes through — during a real",
    "outage, retrying converts one failure into three."
  ],
  "config": {
    "layers": [
      { "name": "sdk", "attempts": 3 },
      { "name": "node", "attempts": 3 },
      { "name": "workflow", "attempts": 3 }
    ],
    "ownership": { "transient": ["sdk"], "node_local": ["node"], "durable": ["workflow"] },
    "reserveBps": 8000,
    "retryBudgetBps": 1000,
    "maxAttemptsPerRun": 8
  },
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "one-owner-per-class-means-no-multiplication",
      "request": {
        "failureClass": "transient",
        "preferredTimeoutMs": 20000,
        "remainingMs": 600000,
        "attemptsUsed": 0,
        "retriesInWindow": 50,
        "callsInWindow": 1000,
        "modelRetries": 1
      },
      "result": {
        "layers": [
          { "name": "sdk", "attempts": 3 },
          { "name": "node", "attempts": 1 },
          { "name": "workflow", "attempts": 1 }
        ],
        "totalCalls": 3,
        "multiplied": false,
        "timeoutMs": 20000,
        "retryAdmitted": true,
        "reason": null
